{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f089a6b7-b01b-4b9a-b435-8b088155129c","agentId":"a084f4b977ecf6d4a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers (mes lib mes-log-mcp/mes; cuore/). Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. No subagents, no COM3; MES logs are read-only at C:\\Program Files (x86)\\MultiEcuScan (the mes catalog reads them); tests use a temp CUORE_STATE_DIR with copies. Minimal grepping. Report under 120 words. Other agents own owner_routes/m_*/labels (print), fullscan/liveboard/scan_health/scanlog (transmission), system_detail_bridge/system.html (network view): do not edit those; you own mes-log-mcp/mes/analysis.py / workup / clear-assessment code (grep -l \"codes_returned_in_session\\|CLEARING STORED\" mes-log-mcp/mes once), cuore/services/dossier_bridge.py (MIL section only, additive), templates/report.html and bench.html (one MIL block each, additive), mes-log-mcp/mes/mechanic_tests.py (additive), cuore/tests/check_mil.py (new). You may commit and push (`github` main only; never koch-mcp/).\n\nFacts: (1) The owner cleared codes with MES on 2026-10-08 09:20 (SCAN_2610080920.txt: 4 DTCs, \"CLEARING STORED FAULT CODES\" at lines 67 and 151; clean SCAN_2610080926 six minutes later). CUORE's dossier still says the last clear was 2026-09-29 10:46 — find why the 8 Oct clear is missed by the clear assessment (second clear marker without \"...\"? a scan with 0 DTCs after? parse order?) and fix it so the newest clear is used everywhere (verdict basis, \"since the clear\" wording, distance/warm-ups since clear reconciliation). (2) Owner states (attested, 2026-10-14): the check-engine lamp on the dash has NOT lit since that clear. (3) The car itself on 2026-10-13 20:03 (from-car readiness observation in C:\\ProgramData\\cuore\\observations.jsonl — copy for tests, never modify): Mode 01 PID 01 reports MIL commanded ON, stored P0440, distance with MIL 34 km, 1663 km since clear, all monitors complete. These conflict: the ECM is requesting the lamp; the owner did not see it.\nBuild \"MIL diagnostics\": a. record the owner's statement as an attested owner event (kind incidents/warning_light_seen with value \"not seen since clear 2026-10-08\", by owner, fields_meta typed) via the owner_events store API (do not edit its files; call it); b. a MIL block on Bench (under the verdict) and Report: \"ECM: MIL commanded ON since <first from-car read showing it>, 34 km with MIL (read from the car 13 Oct 20:03) · Dash lamp: owner reports not lit (attested 14 Oct) · Possible explanations, in order: the cluster did not receive or show the request (IPC has U1736-86/87 history, BCM U1713-2F failing now — the MIL request travels over the bus); lamp/bulb-check failure; owner did not notice. Never state which; each with the test that settles it\"; c. add to mechanic_tests (sourced to SAE J1979 for the MIL command bit, SINGLE-SOURCE for the procedure): mil_bulb_check (key on engine off: the MIL must light for the bulb check — pass/fail), mil_request_vs_lamp (read PID 01 MIL bit with MES/CUORE while looking at the dash; mismatch = cluster/bus path), ipc_mil_status_read (UDS DID on the IPC if one is catalogued, else UNKNOWN DID, not polled); d. the health report and Bench next-action must mention the mismatch as a finding that supports the network hypothesis, hedged (\"consistent with\", never \"cause\"). Tests (check_mil.py, TestClient + fixtures incl. a copy of SCAN_2610080920.txt text): clear assessment picks 2026-10-08 09:20; Bench/Report show the MIL block with both statements and the three explanations; the tests exist with valid keys; no \"cause\"/\"proven\". Run check_mil.py, check_bench.py, check_dossier_page.py, check_tests_page.py, check_screens.py. Commit \"MIL diagnostics: newest MES clear (8 Oct) recognised; ECM MIL request vs dash lamp recorded; bulb-check and request-vs-lamp tests\" with the Co-Authored-By line, push, report hash."},"uuid":"08011390-a9c5-4fb1-a24e-15558c359585","timestamp":"2026-10-14T10:45:24.240Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
