{"parentUuid":"61fe2228-338f-412e-b02f-d92f233ffe07","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a084f4b977ecf6d4a","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg218J3xtMSipgzZWzUdS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NDoRbZqrun8BeJYeVT751g","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\live\\owner_events.py","offset":1,"limit":126},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1381,"cache_read_input_tokens":134833,"output_tokens":316,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":197},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1381},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":316,"cache_read_input_tokens":134833,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1381,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1381,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NDoRbZqrun8BeJYeVT751g":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\live\\owner_events.py","offset":1,"limit":126}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7185d4d3-b6fc-48c4-a8ef-c47da4ecbd9e","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cg218HkrPXbKPqmjpf4EL","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"9b92d2ff-a179-401b-9717-e2821bfd9796","timestamp":"2026-10-14T10:52:12.276Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"9b92d2ff-a179-401b-9717-e2821bfd9796","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f342ac91-4643-4a77-b914-80d2b33b5b32","agentId":"a084f4b977ecf6d4a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NDoRbZqrun8BeJYeVT751g","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"\"Tell CUORE\": what the owner, driver or mechanic reports that the car\n2\tcannot tell CUORE on its own -- a fill-up, a fluid top-up, a pothole hit, a\n3\twindow left open in the rain, a part fitted by another shop.\n4\t\n5\t**This is an ATTESTED record, never a car measurement.** Every row says who\n6\tsaid it, when, at confidence ``\"reported\"`` -- a human claim, kept separate\n7\tfrom, and never promoted into, :mod:`mes.verdict`'s evidence gate. Same\n8\tposture as :mod:`cuore.live.attested` and ``mes.symptoms``: a thing a person\n9\ttyped is evidence that a conversation happened, not evidence the car has a\n10\tfault. See the footer this feature's pages render for the same sentence in\n11\tthe UI.\n12\t\n13\tOne exception, by design, not oversight: a \"noise/smell/vibration noticed\"\n14\treport (category ``incidents``) is not stored here at all -- it is handed to\n15\t``mes.symptoms`` (via :mod:`cuore.services.timeline_bridge`), the store the\n16\tmechanic-vs-driver timeline already reads, so the same report shows up in\n17\tboth places instead of forking into a second, drifting copy. See\n18\t:mod:`cuore.services.owner_events_bridge` for where that hand-off happens.\n19\t\n20\tAppend-only JSONL under ``cuore.live.config.state_dir()`` (``CUORE_STATE_DIR``,\n21\tsame precedence as every other cuore live store), one file,\n22\t``owner_events.jsonl``, three record shapes distinguished by ``op``:\n23\t\n24\t* ``event`` -- {op, id, vin, at, recorded_at, by: {role, name}, category,\n25\t  kind, fields, fields_meta, note, media_ids, odometer_km, confidence=\"reported\"}\n26\t* ``delete``-- {op, id, at} -- marks an event hidden (soft delete)\n27\t* ``restore`` -- {op, id, at} -- undoes a ``delete`` (the Mobile page's own\n28\t  \"Undo\" on the post-delete confirmation screen); folded against ``delete``\n29\t  in append order, so a delete/restore/delete... history is read correctly\n30\t  regardless of how many times it happened\n31\t* ``event_edit`` (added 2026-10-13) -- {op, id, at (the EDIT's own\n32\t  timestamp, never the event's own occurrence time unless ``changes.at``\n33\t  says so), by: {role, name}, changes: {fields: {key: {from, to}},\n34\t  note: {from, to}, odometer_km: {from, to}, at: {from, to}}} -- never\n35\t  rewrites the original ``event`` row; :func:`load` folds every\n36\t  ``event_edit`` for an id onto its ``event`` row, in append order, and\n37\t  keeps the folded result's ``audit`` list (one entry per edit: who, when,\n38\t  what changed) for the UI's disclosure. A changed field's ``fields_meta``\n39\t  becomes ``\"typed\"`` -- it is a hand edit now, even if the field started\n40\t  life as a photo read -- **unless the edit resubmits the exact same value\n41\t  it already had** (\"keeps the photo value\"), in which case the field's\n42\t  existing provenance tag (photo or typed, or none) is left alone.\n43\t\n44\t``fields_meta`` (added 2026-10-13, additive -- older rows simply have none)\n45\tis ``{field_key: \"photo\"|\"typed\"}``, one entry per field whose provenance\n46\tis worth remembering -- \"photo\" for a value read off a picture by the\n47\tMobile \"Snap & fill\" screen (``cuore.web.owner_routes``) rather than typed\n48\tby the person, \"typed\" for an explicit hand-entry note; see that module's\n49\town docstring, and ``cuore.api.owner_events``, for the two callers (the\n50\tHTML form's ``source_<key>=photo`` hidden inputs, and the JSON API's own\n51\t``fields_meta`` body key) that both feed this same parameter. Only a key\n52\tthat is (a) one of this kind's real taxonomy fields and (b) one of these\n53\ttwo words survives into the stored row -- anything else is dropped\n54\tsilently, same posture as an unknown field key ever since this store\n55\texisted. It is informational only: a photo-read field is stored at the\n56\tsame ``confidence: \"reported\"`` as every other owner-typed value (a human\n57\tstill tapped Save) -- this just remembers *how* the value got into the\n58\tbox, for the \"check before saving\" amber chip and for anyone auditing the\n59\treport later.\n60\t\n61\tThis module owns the taxonomy -- the single source of truth the add/list\n62\tform, the API's validation, and the timeline lane all read from -- plus\n63\tplain append/soft-delete/load. Everything that reaches outside ``cuore.live``\n64\t(systems lookups, correlation against DTC history, the feedback/inbox\n65\t\"messages\" bridge) lives in ``cuore.services.owner_events_bridge`` instead,\n66\tsame split ``cuore.live.media`` / nothing-yet-equivalent keeps.\n67\t\"\"\"\n68\t\n69\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n70\t\n71\timport json\n72\timport threading\n73\timport uuid\n74\tfrom datetime import datetime\n75\tfrom pathlib import Path\n76\tfrom typing import Any, Optional\n77\t\n78\tfrom .config import state_dir\n79\t\n80\t_LOCK = threading.Lock()\n81\t\n82\tMAX_NOTE = 4000\n83\tMAX_FIELD_TEXT = 500\n84\t\n85\t#: Who can file a report. ``name`` is optional free text (e.g. \"Dad\", \"Mario\n86\t#: at Midtown Tire\") kept alongside the role.\n87\tBY_ROLES = (\"owner\", \"driver\", \"mechanic\")\n88\t\n89\t\n90\tdef _kind(label: str, fields: dict[str, dict[str, Any]], why_it_matters: str,\n91\t         systems: tuple[str, ...], **relevance: bool) -> dict[str, Any]:\n92\t    \"\"\"One taxonomy entry. ``relevance`` is any of the ``*_relevant`` flags\n93\t    (e.g. ``evap_relevant=True``) -- stored as a dict so a caller can test\n94\t    ``kind[\"relevance\"].get(\"evap_relevant\")`` without a KeyError.\"\"\"\n95\t    return {\n96\t        \"label\": label,\n97\t        \"fields\": fields,\n98\t        \"why_it_matters\": why_it_matters,\n99\t        \"systems\": list(systems),\n100\t        \"relevance\": dict(relevance),\n101\t    }\n102\t\n103\t\n104\tdef _f(type_: str, label: str, *, unit: str = \"\", choices: Optional[tuple[str, ...]] = None,\n105\t      required: bool = False, remember: bool = False) -> dict[str, Any]:\n106\t    \"\"\"One form field descriptor: ``type`` is one of text|number|choice|bool|\n107\t    date|datetime. ``choices`` renders as big tap chips on the mobile form.\"\"\"\n108\t    out: dict[str, Any] = {\"type\": type_, \"label\": label, \"required\": required}\n109\t    if remember:\n110\t        # Free text the garage types again and again (oil brand, filter make,\n111\t        # fuel station): the form offers the values last used, this car first,\n112\t        # then the rest of the garage (see recent_values). Typing stays open.\n113\t        out[\"remember\"] = True\n114\t    if unit:\n115\t        out[\"unit\"] = unit\n116\t    if choices:\n117\t        out[\"choices\"] = list(choices)\n118\t    return out\n119\t\n120\t\n121\t#: category_key -> {label, kinds: {kind_key: _kind(...)}}\n122\t#: The single source the mobile \"Add\" tiles, the API's category/kind\n123\t#: validation, and the timeline owner-events lane all read. Add a kind here\n124\t#: and it is immediately offered on the phone, validated by the API, and\n125\t#: shown on the history page -- nowhere else needs to know about it.\n126\tTAXONOMY: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {"}]},"uuid":"feaaa9d1-51e0-40d7-bef2-1d1a0ecdb1b2","timestamp":"2026-10-14T10:52:12.314Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\live\\owner_events.py","content":"\"\"\"\"Tell CUORE\": what the owner, driver or mechanic reports that the car\ncannot tell CUORE on its own -- a fill-up, a fluid top-up, a pothole hit, a\nwindow left open in the rain, a part fitted by another shop.\n\n**This is an ATTESTED record, never a car measurement.** Every row says who\nsaid it, when, at confidence ``\"reported\"`` -- a human claim, kept separate\nfrom, and never promoted into, :mod:`mes.verdict`'s evidence gate. Same\nposture as :mod:`cuore.live.attested` and ``mes.symptoms``: a thing a person\ntyped is evidence that a conversation happened, not evidence the car has a\nfault. See the footer this feature's pages render for the same sentence in\nthe UI.\n\nOne exception, by design, not oversight: a \"noise/smell/vibration noticed\"\nreport (category ``incidents``) is not stored here at all -- it is handed to\n``mes.symptoms`` (via :mod:`cuore.services.timeline_bridge`), the store the\nmechanic-vs-driver timeline already reads, so the same report shows up in\nboth places instead of forking into a second, drifting copy. See\n:mod:`cuore.services.owner_events_bridge` for where that hand-off happens.\n\nAppend-only JSONL under ``cuore.live.config.state_dir()`` (``CUORE_STATE_DIR``,\nsame precedence as every other cuore live store), one file,\n``owner_events.jsonl``, three record shapes distinguished by ``op``:\n\n* ``event`` -- {op, id, vin, at, recorded_at, by: {role, name}, category,\n  kind, fields, fields_meta, note, media_ids, odometer_km, confidence=\"reported\"}\n* ``delete``-- {op, id, at} -- marks an event hidden (soft delete)\n* ``restore`` -- {op, id, at} -- undoes a ``delete`` (the Mobile page's own\n  \"Undo\" on the post-delete confirmation screen); folded against ``delete``\n  in append order, so a delete/restore/delete... history is read correctly\n  regardless of how many times it happened\n* ``event_edit`` (added 2026-10-13) -- {op, id, at (the EDIT's own\n  timestamp, never the event's own occurrence time unless ``changes.at``\n  says so), by: {role, name}, changes: {fields: {key: {from, to}},\n  note: {from, to}, odometer_km: {from, to}, at: {from, to}}} -- never\n  rewrites the original ``event`` row; :func:`load` folds every\n  ``event_edit`` for an id onto its ``event`` row, in append order, and\n  keeps the folded result's ``audit`` list (one entry per edit: who, when,\n  what changed) for the UI's disclosure. A changed field's ``fields_meta``\n  becomes ``\"typed\"`` -- it is a hand edit now, even if the field started\n  life as a photo read -- **unless the edit resubmits the exact same value\n  it already had** (\"keeps the photo value\"), in which case the field's\n  existing provenance tag (photo or typed, or none) is left alone.\n\n``fields_meta`` (added 2026-10-13, additive -- older rows simply have none)\nis ``{field_key: \"photo\"|\"typed\"}``, one entry per field whose provenance\nis worth remembering -- \"photo\" for a value read off a picture by the\nMobile \"Snap & fill\" screen (``cuore.web.owner_routes``) rather than typed\nby the person, \"typed\" for an explicit hand-entry note; see that module's\nown docstring, and ``cuore.api.owner_events``, for the two callers (the\nHTML form's ``source_<key>=photo`` hidden inputs, and the JSON API's own\n``fields_meta`` body key) that both feed this same parameter. Only a key\nthat is (a) one of this kind's real taxonomy fields and (b) one of these\ntwo words survives into the stored row -- anything else is dropped\nsilently, same posture as an unknown field key ever since this store\nexisted. It is informational only: a photo-read field is stored at the\nsame ``confidence: \"reported\"`` as every other owner-typed value (a human\nstill tapped Save) -- this just remembers *how* the value got into the\nbox, for the \"check before saving\" amber chip and for anyone auditing the\nreport later.\n\nThis module owns the taxonomy -- the single source of truth the add/list\nform, the API's validation, and the timeline lane all read from -- plus\nplain append/soft-delete/load. Everything that reaches outside ``cuore.live``\n(systems lookups, correlation against DTC history, the feedback/inbox\n\"messages\" bridge) lives in ``cuore.services.owner_events_bridge`` instead,\nsame split ``cuore.live.media`` / nothing-yet-equivalent keeps.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport threading\nimport uuid\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\n\nfrom .config import state_dir\n\n_LOCK = threading.Lock()\n\nMAX_NOTE = 4000\nMAX_FIELD_TEXT = 500\n\n#: Who can file a report. ``name`` is optional free text (e.g. \"Dad\", \"Mario\n#: at Midtown Tire\") kept alongside the role.\nBY_ROLES = (\"owner\", \"driver\", \"mechanic\")\n\n\ndef _kind(label: str, fields: dict[str, dict[str, Any]], why_it_matters: str,\n         systems: tuple[str, ...], **relevance: bool) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"One taxonomy entry. ``relevance`` is any of the ``*_relevant`` flags\n    (e.g. ``evap_relevant=True``) -- stored as a dict so a caller can test\n    ``kind[\"relevance\"].get(\"evap_relevant\")`` without a KeyError.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        \"label\": label,\n        \"fields\": fields,\n        \"why_it_matters\": why_it_matters,\n        \"systems\": list(systems),\n        \"relevance\": dict(relevance),\n    }\n\n\ndef _f(type_: str, label: str, *, unit: str = \"\", choices: Optional[tuple[str, ...]] = None,\n      required: bool = False, remember: bool = False) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"One form field descriptor: ``type`` is one of text|number|choice|bool|\n    date|datetime. ``choices`` renders as big tap chips on the mobile form.\"\"\"\n    out: dict[str, Any] = {\"type\": type_, \"label\": label, \"required\": required}\n    if remember:\n        # Free text the garage types again and again (oil brand, filter make,\n        # fuel station): the form offers the values last used, this car first,\n        # then the rest of the garage (see recent_values). Typing stays open.\n        out[\"remember\"] = True\n    if unit:\n        out[\"unit\"] = unit\n    if choices:\n        out[\"choices\"] = list(choices)\n    return out\n\n\n#: category_key -> {label, kinds: {kind_key: _kind(...)}}\n#: The single source the mobile \"Add\" tiles, the API's category/kind\n#: validation, and the timeline owner-events lane all read. Add a kind here\n#: and it is immediately offered on the phone, validated by the API, and\n#: shown on the history page -- nowhere else needs to know about it.\nTAXONOMY: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {","numLines":126,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1084}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9b92d2ff-a179-401b-9717-e2821bfd9796","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
