{"parentUuid":"41e2100a-0215-42e4-9fcb-ef72a2fe92a7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d69f5634-394d-4287-a204-f51c52e3370b","agentId":"a084f4b977ecf6d4a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AsSfCn1xaNpa61hggyyfCp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Mechanic test catalogue: every shop-floor diagnostic test that applies to\n2\tthe 2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0T GME (Giorgio platform), cross-marked for\n3\tthe Giulia 2.0T (same engine/platform family) and the Maserati Grecale 2.0T\n4\t(Giorgio-derived platform, same Stellantis GME-T4 engine family).\n5\t\n6\tSame house rules as :mod:`mes.known_good` / :mod:`mes.systems`: nothing in\n7\there is invented. Every ``pass_criteria`` row carries a ``source`` and a\n8\t``confidence`` --\n9\t\n10\t* ``CONFIRMED``     -- stated in a manufacturer document (FCA/Stellantis\n11\t                       TechAuthority, DOT/FMVSS regulatory standard).\n12\t* ``CORROBORATED``  -- two independent sources agree, or lifted straight\n13\t                       from a ``mes.known_good`` row already carrying that\n14\t                       confidence for this exact channel.\n15\t* ``SINGLE-SOURCE``  -- one source, including a generic/industry-practice\n16\t                       rule of thumb used as an explicit, named fallback\n17\t                       (never confused with a manufacturer figure).\n18\t* ``UNKNOWN``       -- no sourced number exists; the car's own service\n19\t                       manual / TechAuthority is pointed to instead, and\n20\t                       ``spec`` is prose (\"see service manual\"), never a\n21\t                       guessed number. A numeric ``spec`` is never paired\n22\t                       with ``UNKNOWN`` -- enforced at load time below.\n23\t\n24\tFour read-only lookups, the whole public surface:\n25\t\n26\t* :func:`all_tests`        -- every test, as a list.\n27\t* :func:`test`              -- one test by id, or ``None``.\n28\t* :func:`tests_for_codes`   -- tests whose ``related_codes`` match any of\n29\t                               the given DTCs (prefix match, e.g. \"P0455\"\n30\t                               matches a related_codes entry \"P04\").\n31\t* :func:`tests_for_systems` -- tests touching any of the given\n32\t                               :mod:`mes.systems` system ids.\n33\t\n34\tResearch pass done 2026-10-08, same posture as ``known_good.py``'s own\n35\tresearch-pass note: public sources (OBD-II/repair-reference sites, DOT/SAE\n36\tstandards, this repo's own ``mes.known_good``/``mes.systems`` sourced rows)\n37\tplus explicit, named industry-practice rules of thumb where no\n38\tmanufacturer figure exists. No paywalled/bot-gated FCA TechAuthority\n39\tdocument was read for this pass -- every TechAuthority pointer below is a\n40\t\"go get it\", never a claim that document was read.\n41\t\"\"\"\n42\t\n43\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n44\t\n45\tfrom typing import Any, Optional\n46\t\n47\tfrom .systems import CONFIDENCE_LEVELS, CONFIRMED, CORROBORATED, SINGLE_SOURCE, UNKNOWN\n48\tfrom .systems import SYSTEMS\n49\t\n50\t#: Same wording as the rest of this package's UNKNOWN notes.\n51\tTECHAUTHORITY = \"use the service manual, TechAuthority\"\n52\t\n53\t#: Generic/industry-practice rule-of-thumb source label, named explicitly\n54\t#: per instruction -- never confused with a model-specific or\n55\t#: manufacturer-sourced figure.\n56\tINDUSTRY_PRACTICE = \"industry practice\"\n57\t\n58\tCAR_STATES = (\"KOEO\", \"KOER\", \"cold\", \"hot\", \"driving\", \"key-off\")\n59\t\n60\t#: ``not_done`` is a display-only state (no result recorded yet) -- never a\n61\t#: value a caller posts. :data:`POSTABLE_RESULTS` is what a result-recording\n62\t#: call should validate against.\n63\tRESULTS = (\"pass\", \"fail\", \"inconclusive\", \"not_possible\", \"not_done\")\n64\tPOSTABLE_RESULTS = (\"pass\", \"fail\", \"inconclusive\", \"not_possible\")\n65\t\n66\tCATEGORIES = (\n67\t    \"emissions\", \"intake_boost\", \"cooling\", \"fuel\", \"lubrication\",\n68\t    \"leak_detection\", \"mechanical_engine\", \"ignition\", \"electrical\",\n69\t    \"network\", \"brakes\", \"driveline\", \"exhaust\", \"inspection\",\n70\t)\n71\t\n72\t#: Models this catalogue cross-marks, beyond the Stelvio 2018 2.0T this\n73\t#: catalogue is built for -- every test defaults ``True`` for the Stelvio\n74\t#: (the catalogue's whole reason to exist) and is marked per-test for the\n75\t#: other two.\n76\t_MODELS = (\"stelvio_2.0t_2018\", \"giulia_2.0t\", \"grecale_2.0t\")\n77\t\n78\tTESTS: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\n79\t\n80\t_ORDER: list[str] = []\n81\t\n82\t\n83\tdef _applies(giulia: bool = True, grecale: bool = True) -> dict[str, bool]:\n84\t    \"\"\"``stelvio_2.0t_2018`` is always ``True`` -- this whole catalogue is\n85\t    built for that car. ``giulia``/``grecale`` default ``True`` (same\n86\t    engine family / Giorgio-derived platform) and are set ``False`` on the\n87\t    few tests that are genuinely Stelvio/FCA-procedure-specific.\"\"\"\n88\t    return {\"stelvio_2.0t_2018\": True, \"giulia_2.0t\": giulia, \"grecale_2.0t\": grecale}\n89\t\n90\t\n91\tdef _pc(parameter: str, spec: Any, unit: str, source: str, confidence: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n92\t    if confidence not in CONFIDENCE_LEVELS:\n93\t        raise ValueError(f\"bad confidence {confidence!r} for pass_criteria {parameter!r}\")\n94\t    if confidence == UNKNOWN and isinstance(spec, (int, float)):\n95\t        raise ValueError(f\"pass_criteria {parameter!r} has a numeric spec with UNKNOWN \"\n96\t                         \"confidence -- never invent a number\")\n97\t    return {\"parameter\": parameter, \"spec\": spec, \"unit\": unit,\n98\t           \"source\": source, \"confidence\": confidence}\n99\t\n100\t\n101\tdef _t(id_: str, name: str, category: str, systems: list[str], applies_to: dict[str, bool],\n102\t      purpose: str, car_state: str, when_to_use: str, tools: list[str],\n103\t      procedure: list[str], pass_criteria: list[dict[str, Any]], fail_means: str,\n104\t      related_codes: list[str], supports_hypotheses: list[str],\n105\t      refutes_hypotheses: list[str], duration_min: int, safety: str = \"\",\n106\t      hazards: Optional[list[str]] = None) -> None:\n107\t    if id_ in TESTS:\n108\t        raise ValueError(f\"duplicate test id {id_!r}\")\n109\t    if category not in CATEGORIES:\n110\t        raise ValueError(f\"bad category {category!r} for {id_!r}\")\n111\t    for s in systems:\n112\t        if s not in SYSTEMS:\n113\t            raise ValueError(f\"unknown system {s!r} for test {id_!r}\")\n114\t    if car_state not in CAR_STATES:\n115\t        raise ValueError(f\"bad car_state {car_state!r} for {id_!r}\")\n116\t    for key in applies_to:\n117\t        if key not in _MODELS:\n118\t            raise ValueError(f\"unknown model {key!r} in applies_to for {id_!r}\")\n119\t    TESTS[id_] = {\n120\t        \"id\": id_, \"name\": name, \"category\": category, \"systems\": list(systems),\n121\t        \"applies_to\": dict(applies_to), \"purpose\": purpose, \"car_state\": car_state,\n122\t        \"when_to_use\": when_to_use, \"tools\": list(tools), \"procedure\": list(procedure),\n123\t        \"pass_criteria\": list(pass_criteria), \"fail_means\": fail_means,\n124\t        \"related_codes\": list(related_codes), \"supports_hypotheses\": list(supports_hypotheses),\n125\t        \"refutes_hypotheses\": list(refutes_hypotheses), \"duration_min\": duration_min,\n126\t        \"safety\": safety, \"hazards\": list(hazards or []),\n127\t    }\n128\t    _ORDER.append(id_)\n129\t\n130\t\n131\t# ===========================================================================\n132\t# Emissions / EVAP\n133\t# ===========================================================================\n134\t\n135\t_t(\"evap_smoke\", \"EVAP smoke test\", \"emissions\", [\"evap\"], _applies(),\n136\t  purpose=\"Find a leak in the fuel vapor system by filling it with visible/UV smoke \"\n137\t          \"under gentle pressure and watching for where it escapes.\",\n138\t  car_state=\"key-off\",\n139\t  when_to_use=\"P0442/P0455/P0456 or any EVAP small/large leak code, before replacing \"\n140\t              \"any EVAP part on a guess.\",\n141\t  tools=[\"smoke machine\", \"EVAP service port adapter or purge line disconnect\",\n142\t        \"UV light (if using UV dye smoke)\", \"shop light / mirror\"],\n143\t  procedure=[\n144\t      \"Confirm fuel level is in the 15-85% window (vapor space needed to see smoke).\",\n145\t      \"Connect smoke machine to the EVAP system (purge line or service port), low \"\n146\t      \"pressure (~0.5-1 psi / per machine instructions).\",\n147\t      \"Cap the system and let smoke fill for 1-2 minutes.\",\n148\t      \"Inspect gas cap, filler neck, fuel tank seams, EVAP canister, purge/vent valve \"\n149\t      \"connections and hoses for escaping smoke.\",\n150\t      \"Note exact leak location(s); photograph for the job file.\",\n151\t  ],\n152\t  pass_criteria=[_pc(\"visible leak\", \"none found\", \"\", TECHAUTHORITY, UNKNOWN)],\n153\t  fail_means=\"A located, visible leak point identifies the failed component directly \"\n154\t             \"-- no further guessing needed for that leak.\",\n155\t  related_codes=[\"P0442\", \"P0455\", \"P0456\", \"P0457\"],\n156\t  supports_hypotheses=[\"EVAP leak\"], refutes_hypotheses=[\"EVAP leak\"],\n157\t  duration_min=20, safety=\"Use smoke machine per its own manual; do not exceed its \"\n158\t                          \"rated pressure -- EVAP components are not designed for \"\n159\t                          \"boost-level pressure.\",\n160\t  hazards=[\"fuel vapor\"])\n161\t\n162\t_t(\"intake_boost_smoke_leak\", \"Intake/boost leak smoke test\", \"intake_boost\",\n163\t  [\"air_intake_boost\"], _applies(),\n164\t  purpose=\"Find an air leak between the throttle body/MAF and the turbo/intercooler \"\n165\t          \"piping using smoke under light vacuum or low pressure.\",\n166\t  car_state=\"key-off\",\n167\t  when_to_use=\"Rough idle, lean fuel trims, boost-related codes, or a whistle/hiss \"\n168\t              \"under load.\",\n169\t  tools=[\"smoke machine\", \"intake blanking plate or adapter\"],\n170\t  procedure=[\n171\t      \"Block the intake tract at the throttle body (or feed smoke in through a vacuum \"\n172\t      \"port with the engine off).\",\n173\t      \"Fill the tract with smoke at low pressure.\",\n174\t      \"Inspect every clamp, boot, intercooler seam and sensor o-ring for escaping smoke.\",\n175\t      \"Note exact leak location(s).\",\n176\t  ],\n177\t  pass_criteria=[_pc(\"visible leak\", \"none found\", \"\", TECHAUTHORITY, UNKNOWN)],\n178\t  fail_means=\"A located leak point explains lean trims/rough idle/boost loss directly.\",\n179\t  related_codes=[\"P0171\", \"P0101\", \"P0299\", \"P0106\"],\n180\t  supports_hypotheses=[\"intake leak\", \"boost leak\"],"}]},"uuid":"a1e7ac84-21e6-4e37-86c1-987d2b5e9d3f","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:02:20.279Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\mes-log-mcp\\mes\\mechanic_tests.py","content":"\"\"\"Mechanic test catalogue: every shop-floor diagnostic test that applies to\nthe 2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0T GME (Giorgio platform), cross-marked for\nthe Giulia 2.0T (same engine/platform family) and the Maserati Grecale 2.0T\n(Giorgio-derived platform, same Stellantis GME-T4 engine family).\n\nSame house rules as :mod:`mes.known_good` / :mod:`mes.systems`: nothing in\nhere is invented. Every ``pass_criteria`` row carries a ``source`` and a\n``confidence`` --\n\n* ``CONFIRMED``     -- stated in a manufacturer document (FCA/Stellantis\n                       TechAuthority, DOT/FMVSS regulatory standard).\n* ``CORROBORATED``  -- two independent sources agree, or lifted straight\n                       from a ``mes.known_good`` row already carrying that\n                       confidence for this exact channel.\n* ``SINGLE-SOURCE``  -- one source, including a generic/industry-practice\n                       rule of thumb used as an explicit, named fallback\n                       (never confused with a manufacturer figure).\n* ``UNKNOWN``       -- no sourced number exists; the car's own service\n                       manual / TechAuthority is pointed to instead, and\n                       ``spec`` is prose (\"see service manual\"), never a\n                       guessed number. A numeric ``spec`` is never paired\n                       with ``UNKNOWN`` -- enforced at load time below.\n\nFour read-only lookups, the whole public surface:\n\n* :func:`all_tests`        -- every test, as a list.\n* :func:`test`              -- one test by id, or ``None``.\n* :func:`tests_for_codes`   -- tests whose ``related_codes`` match any of\n                               the given DTCs (prefix match, e.g. \"P0455\"\n                               matches a related_codes entry \"P04\").\n* :func:`tests_for_systems` -- tests touching any of the given\n                               :mod:`mes.systems` system ids.\n\nResearch pass done 2026-10-08, same posture as ``known_good.py``'s own\nresearch-pass note: public sources (OBD-II/repair-reference sites, DOT/SAE\nstandards, this repo's own ``mes.known_good``/``mes.systems`` sourced rows)\nplus explicit, named industry-practice rules of thumb where no\nmanufacturer figure exists. No paywalled/bot-gated FCA TechAuthority\ndocument was read for this pass -- every TechAuthority pointer below is a\n\"go get it\", never a claim that document was read.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\n\nfrom .systems import CONFIDENCE_LEVELS, CONFIRMED, CORROBORATED, SINGLE_SOURCE, UNKNOWN\nfrom .systems import SYSTEMS\n\n#: Same wording as the rest of this package's UNKNOWN notes.\nTECHAUTHORITY = \"use the service manual, TechAuthority\"\n\n#: Generic/industry-practice rule-of-thumb source label, named explicitly\n#: per instruction -- never confused with a model-specific or\n#: manufacturer-sourced figure.\nINDUSTRY_PRACTICE = \"industry practice\"\n\nCAR_STATES = (\"KOEO\", \"KOER\", \"cold\", \"hot\", \"driving\", \"key-off\")\n\n#: ``not_done`` is a display-only state (no result recorded yet) -- never a\n#: value a caller posts. :data:`POSTABLE_RESULTS` is what a result-recording\n#: call should validate against.\nRESULTS = (\"pass\", \"fail\", \"inconclusive\", \"not_possible\", \"not_done\")\nPOSTABLE_RESULTS = (\"pass\", \"fail\", \"inconclusive\", \"not_possible\")\n\nCATEGORIES = (\n    \"emissions\", \"intake_boost\", \"cooling\", \"fuel\", \"lubrication\",\n    \"leak_detection\", \"mechanical_engine\", \"ignition\", \"electrical\",\n    \"network\", \"brakes\", \"driveline\", \"exhaust\", \"inspection\",\n)\n\n#: Models this catalogue cross-marks, beyond the Stelvio 2018 2.0T this\n#: catalogue is built for -- every test defaults ``True`` for the Stelvio\n#: (the catalogue's whole reason to exist) and is marked per-test for the\n#: other two.\n_MODELS = (\"stelvio_2.0t_2018\", \"giulia_2.0t\", \"grecale_2.0t\")\n\nTESTS: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\n\n_ORDER: list[str] = []\n\n\ndef _applies(giulia: bool = True, grecale: bool = True) -> dict[str, bool]:\n    \"\"\"``stelvio_2.0t_2018`` is always ``True`` -- this whole catalogue is\n    built for that car. ``giulia``/``grecale`` default ``True`` (same\n    engine family / Giorgio-derived platform) and are set ``False`` on the\n    few tests that are genuinely Stelvio/FCA-procedure-specific.\"\"\"\n    return {\"stelvio_2.0t_2018\": True, \"giulia_2.0t\": giulia, \"grecale_2.0t\": grecale}\n\n\ndef _pc(parameter: str, spec: Any, unit: str, source: str, confidence: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    if confidence not in CONFIDENCE_LEVELS:\n        raise ValueError(f\"bad confidence {confidence!r} for pass_criteria {parameter!r}\")\n    if confidence == UNKNOWN and isinstance(spec, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(f\"pass_criteria {parameter!r} has a numeric spec with UNKNOWN \"\n                         \"confidence -- never invent a number\")\n    return {\"parameter\": parameter, \"spec\": spec, \"unit\": unit,\n           \"source\": source, \"confidence\": confidence}\n\n\ndef _t(id_: str, name: str, category: str, systems: list[str], applies_to: dict[str, bool],\n      purpose: str, car_state: str, when_to_use: str, tools: list[str],\n      procedure: list[str], pass_criteria: list[dict[str, Any]], fail_means: str,\n      related_codes: list[str], supports_hypotheses: list[str],\n      refutes_hypotheses: list[str], duration_min: int, safety: str = \"\",\n      hazards: Optional[list[str]] = None) -> None:\n    if id_ in TESTS:\n        raise ValueError(f\"duplicate test id {id_!r}\")\n    if category not in CATEGORIES:\n        raise ValueError(f\"bad category {category!r} for {id_!r}\")\n    for s in systems:\n        if s not in SYSTEMS:\n            raise ValueError(f\"unknown system {s!r} for test {id_!r}\")\n    if car_state not in CAR_STATES:\n        raise ValueError(f\"bad car_state {car_state!r} for {id_!r}\")\n    for key in applies_to:\n        if key not in _MODELS:\n            raise ValueError(f\"unknown model {key!r} in applies_to for {id_!r}\")\n    TESTS[id_] = {\n        \"id\": id_, \"name\": name, \"category\": category, \"systems\": list(systems),\n        \"applies_to\": dict(applies_to), \"purpose\": purpose, \"car_state\": car_state,\n        \"when_to_use\": when_to_use, \"tools\": list(tools), \"procedure\": list(procedure),\n        \"pass_criteria\": list(pass_criteria), \"fail_means\": fail_means,\n        \"related_codes\": list(related_codes), \"supports_hypotheses\": list(supports_hypotheses),\n        \"refutes_hypotheses\": list(refutes_hypotheses), \"duration_min\": duration_min,\n        \"safety\": safety, \"hazards\": list(hazards or []),\n    }\n    _ORDER.append(id_)\n\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# Emissions / EVAP\n# ===========================================================================\n\n_t(\"evap_smoke\", \"EVAP smoke test\", \"emissions\", [\"evap\"], _applies(),\n  purpose=\"Find a leak in the fuel vapor system by filling it with visible/UV smoke \"\n          \"under gentle pressure and watching for where it escapes.\",\n  car_state=\"key-off\",\n  when_to_use=\"P0442/P0455/P0456 or any EVAP small/large leak code, before replacing \"\n              \"any EVAP part on a guess.\",\n  tools=[\"smoke machine\", \"EVAP service port adapter or purge line disconnect\",\n        \"UV light (if using UV dye smoke)\", \"shop light / mirror\"],\n  procedure=[\n      \"Confirm fuel level is in the 15-85% window (vapor space needed to see smoke).\",\n      \"Connect smoke machine to the EVAP system (purge line or service port), low \"\n      \"pressure (~0.5-1 psi / per machine instructions).\",\n      \"Cap the system and let smoke fill for 1-2 minutes.\",\n      \"Inspect gas cap, filler neck, fuel tank seams, EVAP canister, purge/vent valve \"\n      \"connections and hoses for escaping smoke.\",\n      \"Note exact leak location(s); photograph for the job file.\",\n  ],\n  pass_criteria=[_pc(\"visible leak\", \"none found\", \"\", TECHAUTHORITY, UNKNOWN)],\n  fail_means=\"A located, visible leak point identifies the failed component directly \"\n             \"-- no further guessing needed for that leak.\",\n  related_codes=[\"P0442\", \"P0455\", \"P0456\", \"P0457\"],\n  supports_hypotheses=[\"EVAP leak\"], refutes_hypotheses=[\"EVAP leak\"],\n  duration_min=20, safety=\"Use smoke machine per its own manual; do not exceed its \"\n                          \"rated pressure -- EVAP components are not designed for \"\n                          \"boost-level pressure.\",\n  hazards=[\"fuel vapor\"])\n\n_t(\"intake_boost_smoke_leak\", \"Intake/boost leak smoke test\", \"intake_boost\",\n  [\"air_intake_boost\"], _applies(),\n  purpose=\"Find an air leak between the throttle body/MAF and the turbo/intercooler \"\n          \"piping using smoke under light vacuum or low pressure.\",\n  car_state=\"key-off\",\n  when_to_use=\"Rough idle, lean fuel trims, boost-related codes, or a whistle/hiss \"\n              \"under load.\",\n  tools=[\"smoke machine\", \"intake blanking plate or adapter\"],\n  procedure=[\n      \"Block the intake tract at the throttle body (or feed smoke in through a vacuum \"\n      \"port with the engine off).\",\n      \"Fill the tract with smoke at low pressure.\",\n      \"Inspect every clamp, boot, intercooler seam and sensor o-ring for escaping smoke.\",\n      \"Note exact leak location(s).\",\n  ],\n  pass_criteria=[_pc(\"visible leak\", \"none found\", \"\", TECHAUTHORITY, UNKNOWN)],\n  fail_means=\"A located leak point explains lean trims/rough idle/boost loss directly.\",\n  related_codes=[\"P0171\", \"P0101\", \"P0299\", \"P0106\"],\n  supports_hypotheses=[\"intake leak\", \"boost leak\"],","numLines":180,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1614}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"41e2100a-0215-42e4-9fcb-ef72a2fe92a7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
