{"parentUuid":"d68f1a10-a312-48f7-b6e7-1ad9be8f87ff","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a084f4b977ecf6d4a","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg22j4SkTzD5JpqokhWBe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016AoiayBj7AKh9JgwATS7zN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nMIL diagnostics: newest MES clear (8 Oct) recognised; ECM MIL request vs dash lamp recorded; bulb-check and request-vs-lamp tests\n\n- mes.workup: the clear-assessment logic was anchored to the latest FES\n  session, so a SCAN-only clear with no FES session after it (2026-10-08,\n  4 DTCs cleared, confirmed clean 6 min later) fell outside that window and\n  the dossier kept reporting the stale 2026-09-29 clear. Added a\n  corpus-wide newest-clear scan that supersedes the FES-anchored one, with\n  evidence-based (not string-literal) resolution of a module's blank\n  second clear-result line.\n- Recorded the owner's attested \"MIL not seen since clear\" statement via\n  the owner_events store API (incidents/warning_light_seen).\n- dossier_bridge: additive MIL section comparing the ECM's from-car\n  MIL-commanded state against the owner's attested dash-lamp report;\n  surfaces the mismatch on Bench/Report, hedged with three ordered\n  explanations, each paired with the mechanic_tests entry that settles it.\n- mechanic_tests: added mil_bulb_check, mil_request_vs_lamp and\n  ipc_mil_status_read (honestly UNKNOWN -- no IPC DID catalogued yet).\n- cuore/tests/check_mil.py: new, self-contained checks for all of the above.\nEOF\n)\" && git log -1 --format=\"%H %s\"","description":"Commit the MIL diagnostics feature"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":315,"cache_read_input_tokens":281978,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":315,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","i